-- title:
--   Rational presentation of ℚ̄· F_N over ℚ̄[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive natural number and let $\overline{F}_N$ denote `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, which in turn is the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}(q^{d})$-type expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,\mathrm{jq}$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Write $j \in \overline{F}_N$ for the element given by the coefficientwise embedding of `jq`. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $n$, elements $b_0,\dots,b_{n-1}$ of $\overline{F}_N$, a polynomial $d \in \mathbb{Q}[T]$ and matrices $A_i \in M_n(\mathbb{Q}[T])$ for $i < n$ such that: $n > 0$; $d \neq 0$; for every $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ and every $i$, the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois` attached to $\sigma$ (coefficientwise application of $\sigma$) fixes $b_i$; the $b_i$ are linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j]$, i.e. $\sum_i c_i(j) b_i = 0$ with $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[T]$ forces all $c_i = 0$; every $x \in \overline{F}_N$ satisfies $x\, q(j) = \sum_i c_i(j) b_i$ for some nonzero $q \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[T]$ and some $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[T]$; and the multiplication table $b_i b_j\, d(j) = \sum_k (A_i)_{k j}(j)\, b_k$ holds for all $i,j$, the coefficients of $d$ and of the $A_i$ being mapped from $\mathbb{Q}$ into $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ before evaluation at $j$.
--
--   This provides a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j]$-presentation of the function field of $X_0(N)$ by a Galois-invariant family with a rational multiplication table (all structure constants and the common denominator defined over $\mathbb{Q}$), the shape of data needed for elementary height estimates on the $j$-line. It is used in the treatment of heights on $X_0(N)$, in [`ModularCurve.JZero.chowReciprocity_embedding`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.chowReciprocity_embedding) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.naiveHeight_reduce`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.naiveHeight_reduce).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_rational_presentation_modularFunctionFieldBar.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_QAdicPlace

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
